risk_scan.prompt:
Run a risk scan over the last 24 hours of changes:
1. Use git log/diff to collect changes from the last 24 hours (adds, edits, deletions, and config changes);
2. Identify high-risk issues: runtime errors, data loss, permission bypasses, resource leaks, and cross-platform compatibility problems;
3. For each finding give: file path and line, severity (high/medium/low), root cause, and a fix suggestion.
If nothing was found, state clearly that no high-risk changes were detected. Read-only analysis — do not modify code.

release_notes.prompt:
Draft this week's release notes:
1. Use git log to collect this week's merged PRs and commits (diff against the previous release tag if tags exist);
2. Group them into Features / Fixes / UX improvements / Engineering improvements;
3. Produce two drafts: a detailed team version (with PR/commit references) and a concise user-facing version (no internal details).
Read-only analysis — do not modify code.
